I like art I like making things and  being creative it seems like a uniquely  human thing to do there's been a lot of  talk lately about robots taking our jobs  and I don't doubt that's going to happen  for most jobs I think if you sort of  extrapolate what AI and machines are  good at now - what we can make them good  at it sort of makes sense and I also  agree with the view that robots taking  our jobs is not necessarily a bad thing  because if we can have machines doing  more laborious or monotonous tasks that  frees up sort of a niche for humans to  specialize and the things that machine's  can't do like art writing being creative  which typically we protect as uniquely  human but I also wonder what happens if  you keep extrapolating what we can make  machines do what happens when we can  make AI that can write stories or make  artworks or entertain and give us  content that we consider aesthetically  beautiful what happens when AI are  better artists than humans  I guess there's two options either this  will happen when and we have to deal  with the question of what what do humans  do next what do we have left that that  we could fill or the other option is  that this is never possible that AI will  never be able to be artists I know of at  least one research group who are  currently working on how to teach AI to  write stories how do you break down the  component  of an entertaining narrative into what  can essentially be planned and I  actually think it will be possible  there's already sort of Turing tests for  poetry where there are websites where  you can see a poem that's generated back  by an AI besides a real poem and you  have to try and guess which one was  written by a human and it's actually not  that easy to work it out I think given  enough time we'll probably be able to do  the same thing with stories those  recently talking to someone about what  makes a good story whether it's a movie  or a book or anything else and our  agreement was that sort of the worst  movies we'd seen might have had all the  elements of a successful story like a  love scene a drama an emotional scene or  action but they seemed like accumulation  of all the the best scenes of other  movies there was nothing really unique  about the movie and that made it bad  what I'm saying is that I think the  worst films or movies or stories are  predictable and maybe an AI can be  taught to pick out the best scenes from  all the best things that's been learning  from but maybe an AI generated story can  only ever be predictable on the other  hand if if AI do manage to write or  become great artists what will humans do  I'm not sure I think we really protect  our artistic abilities as what makes us  unique maybe something else we protect  as sort of our identity as humans as the  ability to love so many of our artworks  and stories come down  to the overwhelming feeling of love  maybe that's all we can all we can do  that distinguishes us from AI but maybe  you can teach an AI to love as well I  don't know
 

